History: build 10 and earlier used linux-config-7.2 7.2.9-1 (xz sha256 247d3e6a63e853d87496c1752d6ecb7278e3839bcc3b2277bb7532621864e91f and 1547e1d78ea86c60f62340928f9fb172ee926598f96df00ad00656932ad4aec7).
7.2.9 to 7.2.11 changed in Debian's config only: CONFIG_SENSORS_ARCTIC_FAN_CONTROLLER (not set -> m), CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA512 (m -> y), the new
"# CONFIG_IMA_DEFAULT_HASH_SHA512 is not set", the new CONFIG_CC_OPT_INLINE_MEMSET (written by the compiler probe) and the rustc version lines.

To move to a newer Debian configuration: unpack the new linux-config-7.x package, replace the two files, run
kernel/tests/config-proof.sh for every flavour, and read the table it prints (options that stopped holding, options gone
from the tree, new defaults).
